Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] title: PRESS START is drawn only on the frames the pad is read

STDWTITL_tickMenu starts the "PRESS START" prompt in runPressStart substate 1,
which only counts seven ticks (`timer++ >= 6`) before it moves to substate 2.
STDWTITL_drawMenu runs at the end of every one of those ticks, so the prompt is
on screen from the first tick, but PAD_PRESSED(PAD_START) is read only in
substate 2: a press made in the first seven frames after the prompt appears is
dropped (117 ms at 60 Hz, 140 ms on the 50 Hz EU build; more when the frame
rate dips). Measured on PC: US prompt drawn at frame 54, Start read from 61;
EU 167 and 174; after Return to title the same seven frames.

port/options/title_ready.c decides: the menu does not draw while the original
is still in substate 1 (the check uses the substate at the start of the tick,
so the tick that moves to substate 2 does not draw either: the prompt appears
on the tick whose runPressStart already reads Start). Nothing the player can
press changes, and no press is buffered. On EU the prompt also waits (at most
30 frames) for the logo, which is composed on the first frame its animations
are done and costs 0.24 s on the PC build. The module also logs
`dw3-title: press start shown at frame N, input ready at frame M (cause ...)`.

